how do you sell advertising I got a  question from a facebook reader faith  who's trying to start up a new  publication and is looking for  advertisers and her challenge here is if  she doesn't get advertisers for her  business it's not going to take off  because even if she has great content a  great idea if everything is coming out  of her pocket it's not going to last  it's not going to work because her  pocket is not unlimited  so she needs advertisers to pay for this  thing to help it get off the ground and  she wanted my step-by-step advice on  what to do so faith great question  Congrats we wanted to set up this  business here are a few things for you  really important step-by-step advice to  help guide you along your way the first  thing you want to do to find an  advertiser is you start by making a list  so you think about every single company  that is already advertising to your  target market I always prefer to go with  companies who are who are already  advertising because they have a budget  if you're trying to go to new companies  we've never done any advertising before  it rarely works out because you have to  convince them to start advertising when  they've never done it before it's  possible but it's so much harder  compared to companies who are already  spending a lot of money in your space so  start by making a list of every company  who's advertising to your market now  faith is starting a publication for  homeschooling parents so who's her  target audience in terms of advertisers  anybody who's trying to sell the parents  and it's huge there's so many companies  who are trying to target parents  especially new parents especially young  parents who have you know their first  kids coming out so those are the  comforts of target to find that list  look at any trade shows that deal with  babies or young kids look at any  publications that are already out there  look at any websites that are out there  and just make a list of everybody who's  advertising in there the next thing is  step number two is you want to make a  list of the people who you can contact  at those businesses now this step is a  little bit harder so say for example  pampers is a company you want to target  you need to find somebody at pampers so  you can talk to about your campaign now  who you find really depends on  what your market is going to be so for  your own publication are you looking to  go just for your state just for your  city are you trying to go nationally  trying to go international the person  you connect with that the company will  really depend on what the scope of your  market is going to be so if you're just  trying to do a local regional campaign  something in your state then you need to  find somebody local if you're going for  a national campaign then you get bumped  up the scale a little bit my favorite  way to find people has actually been  through a website called jigsaw comm I'm  not affiliate them in any way other than  being a customer but it's a great way to  find people who work at a specific  company and have a specific job title so  you could go to the website type in  pampers to type in Johnson Johnson type  in marketing or type in advertising and  it'll generate a list of people who work  at that company and if you want to get  their email address you want to get  their phone number then you have to pay  $1 to do it but it's a highly targeted  list and so you can go to the website  and start finding the people who you  need to connect with and you can see  what their title is you don't want to  shoot too high if you're just trying to  do something in your city you don't want  the national advertising manager as you  start to build your list then you get a  targeted group of people who you can  actually connect with and then the next  step is to start reaching out to them  and if it's by email or by phone or by  person you need to start reaching out  and don't hesitate if they start  rejecting you or if they don't respond  to you and that's going to happen  especially at the beginning so the key  elements in making them say yes is  looking at your pitch and if you're  going to break down your pitch I'd say  there are three key things that you need  to remember the first is sustained for  something what is it that makes your  publication so much different better  unique compared to everything else  that's out there because if you're the  same thing as everything else there's no  reason to go with you remember these  advertisers are getting pitched on an  ongoing basis by publications by all  sorts of different outlets trying to get  their money so you need to be different  you need to be unique you need to stand  out and you do that  by standing for something so what do you  stand for are you trying to get more  people to become homeschooling parents  are you trying to make the lives of  homeschooling parents easier what is it  like why are you starting this thing  that's going to come across in your  message if they believe in the same  thing as you do it's going to be so much  easier to convince them to give you  their advertising others that's the  first thing the second thing is show  some momentum a lot of times the people  who are pitching these advertisers have  zero - no momentum they don't have  anything going yet it's really hard to  give dollars to a startup that's never  proven themselves right why am I going  to spend ten thousand dollars five  thousand dollars a thousand dollars  whatever it is with you if you've never  done anything before so show some  momentum wherever you are at in your  progress show that you've done something  show some examples of the stories are  going to write show some examples of the  feedback that's already coming back do  something online create a campaign if  it's on Facebook something to show that  you have a readership base that people  need this thing obviously if you've  already published a few it's easier to  show that but if you haven't done that  yet again show as much momentum as you  can instead of you're saying hey I have  an idea and I'm looking for an  advertiser because you're not going to  get through you've got to show that  you're more than just an idea and then  three find a way to help get them  started at really low cost low  investment and then over deliver like  crazy this one is so important starting  off a new relationship with any company  is always risky it's a risk not just in  terms of their money but also in terms  of their time right they're spending  time with you they're not spending time  with somebody else and they don't want  to make the wrong decision they don't  want to invest their money in the wrong  company and spend their time on projects  that aren't going to work out so because  of that risk they're probably going to  say no and so the way to get them to say  yes is to reduce that risk make it super  easy to get them involved either free or  really minimal commitment at the start  and then over deliver like crazy show  them some results  and as you do that you're going to be  able to increase your prices on  go off and get new advertisers as well  so as an example from my background I I  was hired a number of times to write  blog posts for companies and the first  blog post I wrote they asked me for 250  words 300 words something like that and  instead of just doing that instead of  just doing the bare minimum I wrote like  2,000 words 1,500 words I included a  video I promoted to my audience I got  way more results in what they were  expecting they just wanted me to write  an article and instead I wrote a way  longer article added video content  promoted to my audience  drove tons of traffic to their website  and over delivered like crazy as a  result they hired me back again and  again and again and I increased my  prices that first blog post they paid me  $500 to do now to write a blog post is  $2,500 it's the same content the same  process that I go through but I'm  offering way more value and I can prove  it to them and now when companies ask me  how much is it and I say $2,500 and they  say $2,500 to write one blog post I can  show them what I've done there's a track  record there's a history and so you need  to build that up and so if you go in  right away asking for top dollar they're  probably going to say no so find ways to  reduce that risk at the start so you can  show that you're going to be able to  deliver solid results for them hopefully  that helps if you want send me your  pitch send me what you're sending out  and I'll do a review for you and let you  know what I think of it and where you  can improve because this is so important  it's so important because a lot of  entrepreneurs have these great ideas  have noble ambitions and and doing it  not just for yourself but doing it to  better your community right if this is a  resource that is really lacking in the  homeschooling community then this needs  to get done you need to find a way to  make this happen if you're doing this  just to make money then then I'm not  interested in helping you but if there's  a reason behind that something powerful  something where you want to give back  and have an impact on people then people  can wrap  léa around that and it's so important  that you get this thing done and I don't  want something as simple as finding  advertisers to hold you back from  achieving your dream just because it's  not an area of expertise that you're  really good at with work with effort  with passion you can overcome that  challenge and build a hugely successful  company believe for those of you  watching you liked the video please give  it a thumbs up below and always want to  do more for you and hey I want to hear  we have to think please leave a comment  underneath let me know what you think if  you have a question for your business  leave it below I'll do a video response  thank you guys I'll see you soon
 

